{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/985442-couple-o-questions-involving-attacking-from-the-umbra","id":985442,"title":"Couple o' questions involving Attacking from the Umbra","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-11T08:41:34-07:00","id":985442,"title":"Couple o' questions involving Attacking from the Umbra","content":"its been a while and i been trying to find a gift that my old ST mentioned several times. he called it (rough spanish translation) Spiritual Claws or Spirit Claws.<br /> The way he explained it was &quot;If youre in the umbra/the penumbra, you CANT harm anything that lies on the 'normal realm, you know, where humans live basically' and that you cant physically harm spiritual entities. its like being a ghost.&quot; BUT, other GM told me that if a garou lies within the Penumbra and he attacks a being on the &quot;Other side&quot; (the physical plane), you may directly harm &quot;its soul&quot; and even kill it.<br /> <br /> so...do you need a gift to harm things from the umbra?<br /> do you need a gift in order to attack spirits and banes or you can do it with your claws?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T08:57:26-07:00","id":985448,"title":"","content":"You cannot attack things on one side of the Gauntlet from the other without some sort of Gift. However, some things, like Fomori, exist on both sides and you can harm the whole being even though you're only attacking on one side.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:41:54-07:00","id":985553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/985442-couple-o-questions-involving-attacking-from-the-umbra#post985442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do you need a gift in order to attack spirits and banes or you can do it with your claws?</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou, being half spirit, do not need any special equipment or magic to attack foes in the umbra. A werewolf's claws, fangs, and roundhouse kicks all harm spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T11:54:30-07:00","id":985565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/985442-couple-o-questions-involving-attacking-from-the-umbra?p=985448#post985448\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You cannot attack things on one side of the Gauntlet from the other without some sort of Gift. However, some things, like Fomori, exist on both sides and you can harm the whole being even though you're only attacking on one side.</div> </div> </div> </div>A fomori doesn't exist on both sides of the Gauntlet as an inheret ability. It still would need Powers to affect both sides with a direct action. That his presence is affects the Umbra indirectly not withstanding.<br /> <br /> Besides that, fetishes or other magical means besides gifts can allow to attack trough the Gauntlet.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:07:13-07:00","id":985584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/985442-couple-o-questions-involving-attacking-from-the-umbra?p=985565#post985565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A fomori doesn't exist on both sides of the Gauntlet as an inheret ability. It still would need Powers to affect both sides with a direct action. That his presence is affects the Umbra indirectly not withstanding.<br /> <br /> Besides that, fetishes or other magical means besides gifts can allow to attack trough the Gauntlet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fomori can't <i>attack</i> both sides by default, no. They can be <i>attacked from</i> both sides by default.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-11T12:56:35-07:00","id":985614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>etherial</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/985442-couple-o-questions-involving-attacking-from-the-umbra?p=985584#post985584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fomori can't <i>attack</i> both sides by default, no. They can be <i>attacked from</i> both sides by default.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is incorrect.<br /> <br /> Fomori are 100% physical beings, once the Possession charm has finished (prior to the Possession charm completing, the Bane can be attacked form the Umbra, but afterwards it cannot be). Formori only exist in the Material, outside of possibly special individual fomori.<br /> <br /> Once the fomori dies, the Bane would be released back into the Umbra, where is may be attacked (or flee) normally.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}